  "about": "Launcher contract 1: what OpenBot Desktop 1.1.0, the first app of launcherApi 1 that writes every launcher input this number covers, hands Compose when it starts a release, and which of the server's settings that reaches. Read from this repository at its v1.1.0 tag: desktop/src-tauri/src/env.rs (`compose`, `Ports::default`, `MINTED`, which since 1.1.0 holds OPENBOT_INSTALL_TOKEN), vault.rs (`is_secret`: what goes to Compose's environment instead of .env) and main.rs (`start_stack_inner`: the ports, COMPUTER_NETWORK and OPENBOT_DESKTOP_HOST_TOKEN added to that environment). The person chose an OpenAI key and the local backend; ports are the defaults; the minted secrets are stand-ins of the same shape. `server` is every server setting this launch hands the server through the Compose file of 1.1.0. A record of a released app: what it gives does not change. A release that needs more from the app is a new contract, recorded in launcher-api-<number>.json beside it (scripts/check-launcher-inputs.ts).",
